@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Access Denied";
}
@* Phase 24A (UI/UX stabilization): previously a bare <h1> and one sentence — no shell, no brand,
   no route back. Reached almost always by an already-authenticated caller whose role or
   organization does not extend to the page they tried (the cookie-auth handler only ever routes
   here, rather than to /Account/Login, once a caller is already authenticated), so _Layout.cshtml
   already wraps this in the ordinary sidebar shell; this just needs to look like any other
   FlowOps page rather than raw HTML. Deliberately generic about the reason (CLAUDE.md's own
   authorization posture: never disclose which specific role/organization check failed, since that
   is itself information a caller without access shouldn't get). *@
<div class="page-header">
    <div class="section-head section-head--plain">
        <h1>Access Denied</h1>
        <p class="page-context">You don't have permission to access this page in your current role or organization.</p>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="zone">
    <p class="prose">
        If you believe this is a mistake, confirm you're signed in with the right account, or ask
        an administrator in your organization to check your role.
    </p>
    <p class="page-actions">
        <a class="btn-primary" asp-page="/Index">Back to dashboard</a>
    </p>
</div>
